{%- comment -%}
  Why Subscribe results curve — two series sharing one peak.

  The rise is the shared history: roughly 12 treatments to reach your target
  shade. From that peak the chart branches. Keeping up touch-ups holds the
  shade (navy, flat); stopping lets coffee, staining foods and natural wear
  pull it back down (pink, dashed, declining).

  All text is HTML, never SVG <text> — SVG text scales with the viewBox, which
  previously rendered 10px labels at roughly 30px. Only the curves, wash,
  gridlines, ticks and dots are SVG, with non-scaling-stroke so weights hold
  at any width.

  Two series, so a legend is always present: identity is never carried by
  colour alone. The decline colour sits at 2.54:1 on a light surface, under
  the 3:1 floor, so it is backed by both the legend label and a dashed stroke
  rather than relying on the hue.

  Accepts: points (textarea, one short label per line, up to 4 — start, peak,
           then two points along the branch)
           keep_label / stop_label (legend text)
           highlight (text, one line under the chart)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign lines = points | default: '' | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
{%- assign clean = '' -%}
{%- for line in lines -%}
  {%- assign t = line | strip -%}
  {%- if t != blank -%}
    {%- if clean == '' -%}{%- assign clean = t -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign clean = clean | append: '||' | append: t -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign items = clean | split: '||' -%}

{%- comment -%} Label x positions are fixed to the curve's key points {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign xs = '6,144.6,227.8,314' | split: ',' -%}

<figure class="results-curve">
  <svg
    class="results-curve__svg"
    viewBox="0 0 320 100"
    role="img"
    aria-label="{{ aria | default: 'Shade over time: about twelve treatments to reach your target shade, held with regular touch-ups but fading without them.' | escape }}"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <g class="results-curve__grid" aria-hidden="true">
      <line x1="6" y1="66" x2="314" y2="66"></line>
      <line x1="6" y1="38" x2="314" y2="38"></line>
    </g>
    <line class="results-curve__axis" x1="6" y1="94" x2="314" y2="94" aria-hidden="true"></line>

    {%- comment -%} Wash sits under the maintained line only {%- endcomment -%}
    <path class="results-curve__area" aria-hidden="true" d="M 6.0,94.0 L 9.5,86.6 L 12.9,80.4 L 16.4,75.2 L 19.9,70.6 L 23.3,66.5 L 26.8,62.8 L 30.3,59.5 L 33.7,56.4 L 37.2,53.6 L 40.6,51.0 L 44.1,48.6 L 47.6,46.3 L 51.0,44.1 L 54.5,42.1 L 58.0,40.2 L 61.4,38.3 L 64.9,36.6 L 68.4,34.9 L 71.8,33.3 L 75.3,31.8 L 78.8,30.3 L 82.2,28.9 L 85.7,27.6 L 89.2,26.3 L 92.6,25.0 L 96.1,23.8 L 99.6,22.6 L 103.0,21.5 L 106.5,20.4 L 110.0,19.3 L 113.4,18.3 L 116.9,17.2 L 120.3,16.3 L 123.8,15.3 L 127.3,14.4 L 130.7,13.4 L 134.2,12.5 L 137.7,11.7 L 141.1,10.8 L 144.6,10.0 L 314.0,10.0 L 314.0,94.0 L 6.0,94.0 Z"></path>

    {%- comment -%} Ticks at each labelled point {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for item in items limit: 4 -%}
      <line class="results-curve__tick" x1="{{ xs[forloop.index0] }}" y1="94" x2="{{ xs[forloop.index0] }}" y2="100" aria-hidden="true"></line>
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- comment -%} Decline first, so the maintained line paints over the shared peak {%- endcomment -%}
    <path class="results-curve__line results-curve__line--stop" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" d="M 144.6,10.0 L 148.8,10.1 L 153.1,10.4 L 157.3,10.8 L 161.5,11.2 L 165.8,11.7 L 170.0,12.3 L 174.2,13.0 L 178.5,13.7 L 182.7,14.5 L 187.0,15.3 L 191.2,16.2 L 195.4,17.1 L 199.7,18.1 L 203.9,19.1 L 208.1,20.1 L 212.4,21.2 L 216.6,22.4 L 220.8,23.6 L 225.1,24.8 L 229.3,26.1 L 233.5,27.4 L 237.8,28.7 L 242.0,30.1 L 246.2,31.5 L 250.5,33.0 L 254.7,34.5 L 258.9,36.0 L 263.2,37.5 L 267.4,39.1 L 271.7,40.7 L 275.9,42.4 L 280.1,44.1 L 284.4,45.8 L 288.6,47.6 L 292.8,49.3 L 297.1,51.2 L 301.3,53.0 L 305.5,54.9 L 309.8,56.8 L 314.0,58.7"></path>

    <path class="results-curve__line results-curve__line--keep" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" d="M 6.0,94.0 L 9.5,86.6 L 12.9,80.4 L 16.4,75.2 L 19.9,70.6 L 23.3,66.5 L 26.8,62.8 L 30.3,59.5 L 33.7,56.4 L 37.2,53.6 L 40.6,51.0 L 44.1,48.6 L 47.6,46.3 L 51.0,44.1 L 54.5,42.1 L 58.0,40.2 L 61.4,38.3 L 64.9,36.6 L 68.4,34.9 L 71.8,33.3 L 75.3,31.8 L 78.8,30.3 L 82.2,28.9 L 85.7,27.6 L 89.2,26.3 L 92.6,25.0 L 96.1,23.8 L 99.6,22.6 L 103.0,21.5 L 106.5,20.4 L 110.0,19.3 L 113.4,18.3 L 116.9,17.2 L 120.3,16.3 L 123.8,15.3 L 127.3,14.4 L 130.7,13.4 L 134.2,12.5 L 137.7,11.7 L 141.1,10.8 L 144.6,10.0 L 314.0,10.0"></path>

    {%- comment -%} Start, the shared peak, then each branch end {%- endcomment -%}
    <circle class="results-curve__dot" cx="6" cy="94" r="3.5"></circle>
    <circle class="results-curve__dot results-curve__dot--peak" cx="144.6" cy="10" r="4.5"></circle>
    <circle class="results-curve__dot results-curve__dot--stop" cx="314" cy="58.7" r="4"></circle>
    <circle class="results-curve__dot results-curve__dot--keep" cx="314" cy="10" r="4.5"></circle>
  </svg>

  <div class="results-curve__labels" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- for item in items limit: 4 -%}
      <span class="results-curve__label {% if forloop.index == 2 %}results-curve__label--peak{% endif %}">{{ item | strip }}</span>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Legend: two series, so identity is never colour alone {%- endcomment -%}
  <ul class="results-curve__legend">
    <li class="results-curve__legend-item">
      <span class="results-curve__swatch results-curve__swatch--keep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {{ keep_label | default: 'With touch-ups' }}
    </li>
    <li class="results-curve__legend-item">
      <span class="results-curve__swatch results-curve__swatch--stop" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {{ stop_label | default: 'Without touch-ups' }}
    </li>
  </ul>

  {%- if highlight != blank -%}
    <figcaption class="results-curve__highlight body-xs">{{ highlight }}</figcaption>
  {%- endif -%}
</figure>
